      "text": "To determine the day of the week on December 23 given that Thanksgiving is on Thursday, November 23, we need to calculate the number of days between November 23 and December 23 and then determine the day of the week that corresponds to these days.\n\nFirst, let's count the number of days between November 23 and December 23:\n\n- November has 30 days.\n- Since November 23 is the start day, we need to count 30 days from November 23.\n- December has 31 days, so we need to count an additional 31 days in December.\n\nAdding these together, we get:\n\\[ 30 \\text{ days in November} + 31 \\text{ days in December} = 61 \\text{ days} \\]\n\nNext, we need to determine the day of the week that is 61 days after Thursday. We do this by calculating the remainder when 61 is divided by 7, since there are 7 days in a week.\n\n\\[ 61 \\div 7 = 8 \\text{ remainder } 5 \\]\n\nThis means that 61 days is equivalent to 8 weeks and 5 days, with 5 days being the remainder. Since we start on Thursday, adding 5 days to Thursday gives us the following:\n\\[ \\text{Thursday} + 5 \\text{ days} = \\text{Sunday} \\]\n\nTherefore, the day of the week on December 23 is \\(\\boxed{\\text{Sunday}}\\).",
