      "text": "1. **Determine the number of days in the span:**\n   Since there are 9 days between November 23 and December 23, we must determine whether this period includes a leap year.\n   \n2. **Analyze leap year implications:**\n   To find out if there is a leap year in the 11-month span, count the total number of days and check for whether any of these days fall on a leap day (February).\n   - The number of days in 11 months is \\(30 + 31 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 31 + 30 + 28 + 29\\).\n   - There will be 31 in the months where is leap and hence number of leap days will be 1.\n\n3. **Count the total number of days and evaluate:**\n   We see 31 = 2 + 1 leap day (February).\n   - Therefore, total number of days = 26 + (2 + 1) = 29 days.\n   \n4. **Determine total day of the week shift and extract day number:**\n   From November 23 to any day after, shift will cause total of 2 days forward.\n   Therefore, November 23 to December 23 has a total of  31 + 2 days which is a total of 33 days shift.\n   As per the rule 33 days shift of the week goes complete shift of a week.\n   Therefore, the day 2 days back from December 23 to November 23 will be fourth of last day of this week after that day.\n   Hence, December 23 is on the day of Monday.\n\nSo, December 23 falls on \\(\\boxed{\\text{Monday}}\\) given that first week of December is Friday.",
